The table shows data from paleontologist Angélica Torices and colleagues'' 2021 study of two sets of dinosaur
tracks preserved in a fossilized lake bed in Spain. The tracks, referred to as La Torre 6A and La Torre 6B, were left
by two individual theropods (dinosaurs that walked on two legs). The team''s findings suggest that of the two
theropods, the one that left the La Torre 6B tracks had a higher maximum mean speed,', '["a longer footprint, and a longer average stride.", "a longer footprint, and a shorter average stride.", "a shorter footprint, and a longer average stride.", "a shorter footprint, and a shorter average stride."]', 2, 'The correct answer is C. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (481, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'easy', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?', 'Average Temperatures in July in Four Locations in the Navajo Nation
