When magma moves underneath a volcano, it causes the surface of the volcano to change. This is known as
deformation. Researchers recently calculated the amount of deformation occurring each month for five volcanoes
in Latin America. Although Sierra Negra experienced a lot of deformation, its deformation rate was still lower than
that of', '["Alcedo.", "Pacaya.", "Fernandina.", "Maule."]', 1, 'The correct answer is B. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (499, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'medium', 'Which choice best describes data from the table that support Chung and colleagues'' conclusion?', 'Effect of Paywall Introduction on Newspaper Companies'' Revenues
