Researchers Carolina Laura Morales and Anna Traveset gathered data about flowering plants growing alongside each other
in various locations. In each case, the researchers identified one plant as a "target species" and a nearby plant as a
"neighboring species." The researchers then calculated a positive or negative value to show how the neighboring species
affected pollinator visits to the target species. One example of a neighboring species with a negative effect value is the', '["Himalayan balsam.", "common dandelion.", "star chickweed.", "Virginia spring beauty."]', 1, 'The correct answer is B. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (517, 'reading_writing', 1, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'medium', 'Which finding, if true, would most directly support the underlined claim?', 'The Minneapolis Institute of Art in Minneapolis, Minnesota, has over 90,000 works of art. Digital images of thousands of
those works have been put online through the museum''s website and the Google Arts & Culture project. One of the images is
of Mississippi Delta, a drawing by Siah Armajani. In a paper, a student claims that putting a work from the museum online
increases the number of people who experience that work.', '["The Minneapolis Institute of Art has several works by Siah Armajani.", "Many people who have been to Minneapolis say that the Minneapolis Institute of Art is worth visiting.", "Mississippi Delta has been praised by some art critics.", "Each year, more people access the online image of Mississippi Delta than visit the Minneapolis Institute of Art in person."]', 3, 'The correct answer is D. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (518, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'medium', 'Which quotation from "We Are Marching" most effectively illustrates the claim?', '"We Are Marching" is a 1921 poem by Carrie Law Morgan Figgs. In the poem, the speaker predicts future success: ____', '["\"Can''t you hear the sound of feet?\"", "\"You who are out just get in line.\"", "\"We have answered duty''s call.\"", "\"We shall never know defeat.\""]', 3, 'The correct answer is D. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
