The Jordanelle Dam was built on the Provo River in Utah in 1992. Earth scientist Adriana E. Martinez and
colleagues tracked changes to the environment on the banks of the river downstream of the dam, including how
much grass and forest cover were present. They concluded that the dam changed the flow of the river in ways
that benefited grass plants but didn''t benefit trees.', '["The lowest amount of grass cover was approximately 58,000 square meters, and the highest amount of forest cover was approximately 75,000 square meters.", "There was more grass cover than forest cover in 1987, and this difference increased dramatically in 1993 and again in 2006.", "There was less grass cover than bare soil in 1987 but more grass cover than bare soil in 1993 and 2006, whereas there was more forest cover than bare soil in all three years.", "Grass cover increased from 1987 to 1993 and from 1993 to 2006, whereas forest cover decreased in those periods."]', 3, 'The correct answer is D. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 90, '[]');
