To test the effects of a nitrogen fertilizer on cantaloupe production, researchers grew cantaloupe plants and
harvested their fruit over three years. In each year, half the plants were grown using a nitrogen fertilizer, and the
other half were grown using a control fertilizer that contained no nitrogen. The researchers concluded that the
nitrogen fertilizer increases cantaloupe yield.', '["In every year of the experiment, plants treated with the nitrogen fertilizer had a yield of at least 30 pounds per acre.", "In every year of the experiment, plants treated with the nitrogen fertilizer had a greater yield than did plants treated with the control fertilizer.", "The 2018 yield for plants treated with the control fertilizer was greater than was the 2019 yield for plants treated with the nitrogen fertilizer.", "The yield for plants treated with the nitrogen fertilizer increased from 2017 to 2018."]', 1, 'The correct answer is B. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (547, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'hard', 'Which quotation from An Ideal Husband most effectively illustrates the claim?', 'An Ideal Husband is an 1895 play by Oscar Wilde. In the play, which is a satire, Wilde suggests that a character
named Lady Gertrude Chiltern is perceived as both extremely virtuous and unforgiving, as is evident when
another character says', '["\"Lady Chiltern is a woman of the very highest principles, | am glad to say. | am a little too old now, myself, to trouble about setting a good example, but | always admire people who do.\"", "\"Do you know, [Lady Chiltern], | don''t mind your talking morality a bit. Morality is simply the attitude we adopt towards people whom we personally dislike.\"", "\"[Lady Chiltern] does not know what weakness or temptation is. | am of clay like other men. She stands apart as good women do\u2014pitiless in her perfection\u2014cold and stern and without mercy.\"", "\"Lady Chiltern, you are a sensible woman, the most sensible woman in London, the most sensible woman | know.\""]', 2, 'The correct answer is C. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (548, 'reading_writing', 1, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'hard', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the text?', 'Five of the Responses to Survey about Actions to Conserve Energy
