Aerial robots vary considerably in their holding force; the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand, for example, has a holding force
of 56 newtons, more than twice that of the Permanent Magnet Hand and more than four times that of the Yale
Model T. Since an aerial robot must lift its own weight along with its cargo, engineer Jiawei Meng and colleagues
used a ratio of each robot''s holding force to the robot''s weight to calculate payload capacity, with higher ratios
corresponding to greater capacity, concluding that the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand has a higher payload capacity than
the Yale Model T.', '["The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand and the Yale Model T each weigh more than 450 grams.", "The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand and the Yale Model T each weigh more than the Permanent Magnet Hand does.", "The Yale Model T has a lower holding force than the Permanent Magnet Hand despite weighing more.", "The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand weighs only slightly more than the Yale Model T does."]', 3, 'The correct answer is D. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (581, 'reading_writing', 1, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'hard', 'Which quotation from Electra most effectively illustrates the claim?', 'Electra is a circa 420-410 BCE play by Sophocles, translated in 1870 by R.C. Jebb. Electra, who is in mourning for
her dead father and her long-absent brother, is aware of the intensity of her grief but believes it to be justified:', '["\"O thou pure sunlight, and thou air, earth''s canopy, how often have ye heard the strains of my lament, the wild blows dealt against this bleeding breast, when dark night fails!\"", "\"Send to me my brother; for | have no more the strength to bear up alone against the load of grief that weighs me down.\"", "\"| know my own passion, it escapes me not; but, seeing that the causes are so dire, will never curb these frenzied plaints, while life is in me.\"", "\"But never will | cease from dirge and sore lament, while | look on the trembling rays of the bright stars, or on this light of day.\""]', 2, 'The correct answer is C. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (582, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'hard', 'Which choice uses data from the table to most effectively support the researchers'' conclusion?', 'Tadpole Body Mass and Toxin Production after Three Weeks in Ponds
