Economist Steve H. Hanke has shown that divided US Congresses—which occur when one party holds the
majority in the House of Representatives and another holds the majority in the Senate—tend to accompany
reductions in total federal outlays (Spending) relative to gross domestic product (GDP), which Hanke interprets to
reflect decreases in government size. Hanke calculated the percentage point change in total outlays
(encompassing nondefense and defense outlays) for consecutive US Congresses. Hanke has pointed to his
calculations as evidence that a divided Congress may be a "necessary but not sufficient condition" for a decrease
in government size to occur.', '["The periods of undivided Congresses were associated with increases in nondefense outlays, whereas all the periods of divided Congresses except one were associated with reductions in defense outlays.", "All the periods of divided Congresses were associated with reductions in total outlays, although two periods were also associated with increases in nondefense outlays.", "The periods of undivided Congresses were associated with increases in total outlays, whereas all the periods of divided Congresses were associated with reductions in either nondefense outlays or defense outlays.", "All the periods of divided Congresses except one were associated with reductions in total outlays, whereas the periods of undivided Congresses were associated with increases in total outlays."]', 3, 'The correct answer is D. This question requires understanding of command of evidence concepts.', 'This question tests your understanding of Command of Evidence. Information and Ideas is one of the key content domains on the SAT.', 'Practice more Command of Evidence problems to strengthen your skills in this area.', 0, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (588, 'reading_writing', 2, 'information_ideas', 'evidence', 'hard', 'Which choice best describes data from the table that support Egoh and colleagues'' assertion?', 'Distribution of Ecosystem Services Affected by Invasive Species by Service Type
Region (Overall) | Provisioning (75%) | Regulating (21%) | Cultural (4%)
