y = 3x + a 
In the given system of equations, a is a constant. The 
graphs of the equations in the given system intersect 
at exactly one point, ( ,x y), in the x y-plane. What is 
the value of x ?', NULL, '["\u22128", "\u22126", "6", "8"]', 2, 'Choice C is correct. It''s given that the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, ( ) , x y , in the xy-plane. Therefore, ( ) , x y is the only solution to the given system of equations. The given system of equations can be solved by subtracting the second equation, 3 y x a = + , from the first equation, 2 2 21 64 y x x = - + . This yields ( ) ( ) 2 2 21 64 3 y y x x x a - = - + - + , or 2 0 2 24 64 x x a = - + - . Since the given system has only one soluti...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '["has_figure"]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1328, 'math', 1, 'algebra', 'linear_equations_one_var', 'advanced', 'What is a solution to the given equation?', NULL, '["6", "30", "450", "900"]', 2, 'Choice C is correct. Since the triangle is an isosceles right triangle, the two sides that form the right angle must be the same length. Let x be the length, in inches, of each of those sides. The Pythagorean theorem states that in a right triangle, 2 2 2 a b c + = , where c is the length of the hypotenuse and a and b are the lengths of the other two sides. Substituting x for a, x for b, and 58 for c in this equation yields 2 2 2 58 x x + = , or 2 2 2 58 x = . Dividing each side of th...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1329, 'math', 1, 'advanced_math', 'nonlinear_equations', 'advanced', 'In the x y-plane, a parabola has vertex (9, −14) and 
