 ?', NULL, '["\u221223", "\u221219", "\u221214", "\u221212"]', 3, 'Choice D is correct. The equation of a parabola in the xy-plane can be written in the form ( ) 2 y a x h k = - + , where a is a constant and ( ) , h k is the vertex of the parabola. If a is positive, the parabola will open upward, and if a is negative, the parabola will open downward. It''s given that the parabola has vertex ( ) 9, 14 - . Substituting 9 for h and 14 - for k in the equation ( ) 2 y a x h k = - + gives ( ) 2 9 14 y a x = - - , which can be rewritten as ( )( ) 9 9 14 y a x...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
