II. g(x) = −3(6)x', NULL, '["I only", "II only", "I and II", "Neither I nor II"]', 3, 'Choice D is correct. A function of the form f x a b c x = + ^ ^ h h , where a 0 1 and b 1 2 , is a decreasing function. Both of the given functions are of this form; therefore, both are decreasing functions. If a function f is decreasing, as the value of x increases, the corresponding value of f x ^ h decreases; therefore, the function doesn''t have a minimum value. Thus, neither of the given functions has a minimum value.', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
