following could be the measure, in degrees, of ∠S ?', NULL, '["116", "118", "126", "180"]', 0, 'Choice A is correct. The sum of the measures of the angles of a triangle is ° 180 . Therefore, the sum of the measures of R + , S + , and T + is ° 180 . It''s given that the measure of R + is ° 63 . It follows that the sum of the measures of S + and T + is ° 180 63 - ^ h , or ° 117 . Therefore, the measure of S + , in degrees, must be less than 117. Of the given choices, only 116 is less than 117. Thus, the measure, in degrees, of S + could be 116.', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
