What is the median of the data set shown?', NULL, '["4", "5", "7", "14"]', 1, 'Choice B is correct. If a data set contains an even number of data values, when the data values are listed in ascending or descending order, the median is between the two middle values. The given data set contains 8 values. When listed in ascending order, the data set is 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 6, 10, 18 and the two middle values are 5 and 5. Since the two middle values are the same, the median must be 5.', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1518, 'math', 2, 'geometry', 'area_volume', 'hard', 'A right circular cylinder has a volume of 432 cubic 
centimeters. The area of the base of the cylinder is 
24 square centimeters. What is the height, in 
centimeters, of the cylinder?', NULL, '["18", "24", "216", "10,368"]', 0, 'Choice A is correct. The volume, V, of a right circular cylinder is given by the formula V r h 2 r = , where r2 r is the area of the base of the cylinder and h is the height. It''s given that a right circular cylinder has a volume of 432 cubic centimeters and the area of the base is 24 square centimeters. Substituting 432 for V and 24 for r2 r in the formula V r h 2 r = yields h 432 24 = . Dividing both sides of this equation by 24 yields h 18= . Therefore, the height of the cylinder, in...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
