this area?', NULL, '["18", "131", "149", "2,376 42 - --------~ - ---- y \\ 12 I \\ 11 I \\ 10 I \\ 9 I \\ 8 I \\ 7 I '' 6 I"]', 0, 'Choice A is correct. It''s given that there are , 2 358 raccoons in a 131-square-mile area. The estimated population density, in raccoons per square mile, is the estimated number of raccoons divided by the number of square miles. Therefore, the estimated population density of this area is , square miles raccoons 131 2 358 , or 18 raccoons per square mile.', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 120, '[]');
