equations is given. The system has no solution.
Which equation could be the second equation in the
system?', NULL, '["x y \u22126 + = 18", "x y \u22126 + = 22", "x y \u221212 + = 36", "x y \u221212 + = 18"]', 1, 'Choice B is correct. A system of two linear equations in two variables, x and y, has no solution if the lines represented by the equations in the xy-plane are parallel and distinct. Lines represented by equations in standard form, Ax By C + = and Dx Ey F + = , are parallel if the coefficients for x and y in one equation are proportional to the corresponding coefficients in the other equation, meaning 47 A D B E = ; and the lines are distinct if the constants are not proportional, meaning C...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
