For which of the following tables are all the values of
x and their corresponding values of y solutions to the
given inequality?', NULL, '["x 3 y 17 5 27 7 37", "x y 3 17 5 35 7 37", "x y 3 25 5 35 7 45", "x 3 y"]', 0, 'Choice A is correct. Substituting 3 for x in the given inequality yields y 5 3 6 < + ^ h , or y 21 < . Therefore, when x 3 = , the corresponding value of y is less than 21. Substituting 5 for x in the given inequality yields y 5 5 6 < + ^ h , or y 31 < . Therefore, when x 5 = , the corresponding value of y is less than 31. Substituting 7 for x in 37 the given inequality yields y 5 7 6 < + ^ h , or y 41 < . Therefore, when x 7 = , the corresponding value of y is less than 41. For the ...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 150, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1826, 'math', 1, 'geometry', 'right_triangles_trig', 'hard', 'A right triangle has legs with lengths of
24 centimeters and 21 centimeters. If the length of
this triangle''s hypotenuse, in centimeters, can be
written in the form
