What is the positive solution to the given equation?', NULL, '["3", "4", "9", "72"]', 0, 'Choice A is correct. It''s given that each participant earns 1 point for each game the participant plays that ends in a draw and 3 points for each game the participant wins. Since d represents the number of games that a certain participant has played that ended in a draw and w represents the number of games this participant has won, this participant has earned a total of d w 1 3 + , or d w 3 + , points. Since this participant earned 41 points, the equation d w 3 41 + = represents this situa...', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 120, '[]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1907, 'math', 1, 'problem_solving', 'ratios_rates', 'medium', '[See practice test 11 PDF — Math Module 1, Question 12]', NULL, '["A", "B", "C", "D"]', 1, 'Choice B is correct. The point ^x, y h at which the graphs of the given equations
intersect is the solution to the system of equations. Subtracting 5 from both sides
of the equation x + 5 = 14 yields x = 9. Substituting 9 for x in the equation
y = 4x 2 + 4 yields y = 4^9h2 + 4, or y = 328. Therefore, the graphs of the
equations in the given system intersect at the point ^9, 328h.
Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.
Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.', 'This is a College Board practice test question. Review the official explanation for detailed analysis.', 'Work through more practice test questions in this section to build familiarity with the test format.', 1, 120, '["figure_required"]');
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, module, topic, subtopic, difficulty, question_text, passage_text, options, correct_index, explain_why, explain_concept, explain_next, is_calculator_allowed, est_time_sec, tags) VALUES (1908, 'math', 1, 'problem_solving', 'one_var_data', 'hard', 'A scientist measured the lengths of 240 gray seals 
from Muskeget Island and 120 gray seals from Sable 
Island. The scientist determined that the mean 
length of the 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island 
